# kmet lsp-adapter extension — implementation plan (Phase 1)

Status: **planned**. This document is the design contract; deviations during
implementation must be reflected back here (§18).

Design sources:

- **[dirge](file:///home/u0_a766/src/cvstree/dirge)** — local checkout
  `~/src/cvstree/dirge/src/lsp/` is the authoritative behavioral reference
  (read the .rs modules named in §4 before implementing each counterpart).
  Dirge itself mirrors opencode's `tool/lsp.ts` agent surface.
- **extensions/mcp-adapter** — the structural template: EDN config pair,
  locked idempotent connect + failure backoff, idle-reaper daemon, command
  surface, footer status, validation-scripts harness.

## 1. Goal

Give the agent semantic code intelligence (definition, references, hover,
symbols, call hierarchy, diagnostics) through **one ~150-token `lsp` tool**,
speaking the Language Server Protocol to lazily-spawned stdio servers.
Servers start only when a claimed file is actually queried — same
context-economy pitch as mcp-adapter, applied to code navigation: `grep`
finds text, `lsp` finds meaning.

Immediately useful target: `clojure-lsp` on this very repo (root marker
`deps.edn`). Everything is best-effort per server: a missing binary is a
status line, never an error at startup.

## 2. Locked decisions

| Decision | Choice |
|---|---|
| Design source | dirge `src/lsp/*` — behavioral parity wherever feasible; structure follows `extensions/mcp-adapter` |
| Scope | Phase 1 only (see §3); Phase 2 items specified but not built |
| Tool name | `lsp` — one proxy-style tool with an `operation` enum (dirge/opencode surface); no direct tools |
| Transports | **stdio only** — LSP reality; no HTTP/SSE (the complexity budget goes to Content-Length framing + server→client requests instead) |
| Config format | EDN only — exactly two files: global `~/.kmet/agent/lsp.edn`, project `.kmet/lsp.edn` (project wins) |
| Shared machinery | new lib **`kmet.libs.jsonrpc`** (framing + correlation + dispatch); mcp-adapter is **untouched** in Phase 1 (adoption recorded as optional follow-up, §3) |
| Server discovery | builtin registry (dirge's set) reshaped by config; user adds out-of-tree servers in `lsp.edn` |
| Workspace roots | marker walk-up from the queried file, bounded by cwd (port of dirge `nearest_root`) |
| Coordinates | the tool takes **1-based** line/character (editor convention); conversion to 0-based wire format lives in exactly one place (`query.clj`) |
| Writes | out of scope — no rename/codeAction/formatting/applyEdit (an extension silently rewriting files is a policy question; `workspace/applyEdit` is *refused* by policy, see §9.4) |
| Entry ns | `extensions.lsp-adapter` (a `kmet.*` prefix is rejected by the loader) |

## 3. Scope

### In scope (Phase 1)

- EDN config loading/merging/template/write-back (§6)
- New shared lib `kmet.libs.jsonrpc`: both framings (content-length,
  line-delimited), correlation core, server-request/notification dispatch,
  graceful-shutdown parameterization, stderr tails (§8)
- Builtin server registry + language detection + workspace-root resolution
  (§7)
- LSP client layer: initialize handshake, conservative capabilities,
  server-request policy, notification routing, document-sync builders (§9)
- Manager: lazy spawn keyed `(server, root)` with dedupe locks, broken-server
  backoff, document sync (full-text), fan-out operations, idle reaper (§10)
- The `lsp` tool: 10 operations incl. `diagnostics` (§11)
- Diagnostics store + pretty printing (push-collect only) (§12)
- Entry: init/shutdown, `/lsp` command, footer status, events (§13)
- Validation scripts + README (§14, §15)

### Phase 2 (specified, not built)

- **Diagnostics-after-edit hook** (§12.3): `on-tool-result` on `edit`/`write`
  appends fresh `<diagnostics>` to the tool result (dirge Phase-6 parity).
- Interactive panel (`/lsp` plain dialog stays; a pi-McpPanel-style TUI panel).
- Incremental text sync (`TextDocumentSyncKind.Incremental`) if full-text
  sync ever shows up in profiling.
- Pull-diagnostics race in the after-edit wait (dirge B3-10).
- Optional cleanup: refactor mcp-adapter's stdio transport onto
  `kmet.libs.jsonrpc` (churn-vs-dedup judged not worth destabilizing a
  shipped extension in Phase 1).

### Out of scope

- Rename / codeAction / formatting / completion / `workspace/applyEdit`
  acceptance — the agent edits files itself through kmet's own tools.
- HTTP/socket LSP transports (no ecosystem demand).
- Multi-root workspaces (one root per `(server, file)` resolution).

## 4. Port mapping (dirge → kmet)

| dirge module | kmet file | Ported behavior |
|---|---|---|
| `src/lsp/rpc.rs` + shared `jsonrpc_client` core | **`kmet.libs.jsonrpc`** | framing (content-length), correlation (pending-by-id), server-request dispatch, drain-on-close — dirge already factored this core out; we do the same up front |
| `src/lsp/language.rs` | `language.clj` | extension/filename → languageId tables, `"plaintext"` fallback |
| `src/lsp/server.rs` | `servers.clj` | builtin descriptors (id, claims, root markers), `nearest_root` walk-up with include/exclude markers + boundary fallback, rust `[workspace]` special case, deno hand-off exclusion, config override semantics (`:extensions` replaces / `:extend-extensions` additive / `:disabled` removes) |
| `src/lsp/spawn.rs` | `kmet.libs.process` + client | spawn abstraction collapses into the lib's `connect-stdio`; tree-kill via existing lib |
| `src/lsp/init.rs` | `client.clj` | initialize handshake params, conservative client capabilities, `initialized` ack |
| `src/lsp/client.rs` | `client.clj` + `manager.clj` | document-sync message builders, capability introspection |
| `src/lsp/manager.rs` | `manager.clj` | lazy spawn per `(root, server-id)` with in-flight dedupe, broken-server backoff, touch_file sync, fan-out ops, `shutdown_all`, active/broken reporting |
| `src/lsp/query.rs` | `query.clj` | operation parsing + camelCase aliases, op→method mapping, the single 1-based→0-based coordinate conversion, "(no results)" convention |
| `src/lsp/diagnostic.rs` | `diagnostics.clj` | severity names, 1-based rendering, caps (8/file, flood 40 → summary, ≤5 project files) |
| `src/agent/tools/lsp.rs` | `lsp_adapter.clj` + `query.clj` | tool description, parameter schema (operation/file_path/line/character/query), result shaping philosophy |

Deliberately not ported from dirge: the plugin harness bridge (`harness.rs`),
the `TouchMode::AwaitPush` diagnostic wait (Phase 2), the pull-diagnostics
race (Phase 2), worktree-permission path guarding (extensions have no
worktree concept — cwd bounds the walk instead), and the `[timeouts]` config
subsystem (flat settings keys here), and mcp-adapter's credential-url
binding rule (its §6 SECURITY) — LSP config carries no credential fields
by convention (`:env` aside); adopt the rebinding rule if that ever
changes.

From mcp-adapter, reused by copy (extensions cannot require each other):

| mcp-adapter piece | Destination | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `config.clj` mechanics | `config.clj` | built on the **existing** `kmet.libs.edn-store` primitives (`deep-merge`, `read-edn-map`, `update-edn-map!` under lock, `pretty-edn`) — no new config lib; extension-local remainder is only the camel/kebab alias list, the two-file load composition, and the entry write-back glue. Note: mcp-adapter currently re-implements these primitives instead of using edn-store — optional future cleanup alongside the jsonrpc adoption |
| §10.3 `ensure-connected!` + failure backoff | `manager.clj` | locked idempotent connect, `:failed-at` window, explicit-restart bypass |
| idle-reaper daemon | `lsp_adapter.clj` | same 30s daemon-thread shape |
| output-guard *idea* | `query.clj`/`diagnostics.clj` | LSP shaping is semantic (locations/symbols/hover), not byte-guards |
| scripts/ harness pattern | `scripts/` | fake server + validators + e2e |
| daemon-thread helper (`spawn`) | each ns needing it | futures don't exist in the extension sci context — ~7-line helper, copied |

## 5. File layout

New core files (inside the `bb lint`/`bb test` gates):

```
src/kmet/libs/jsonrpc.clj           NEW shared lib — framing + correlation + stdio client
test/kmet/libs/jsonrpc_test.clj     NEW lib unit tests (runner-registered)
```

The extension (outside the gates — lint manually, clj-kondo-clean anyway):

```
extensions/lsp-adapter/
├── extension.edn                 {:name "lsp-adapter" :entry "src/extensions/lsp_adapter.clj"}
├── README.md                     usage, config reference, /lsp reference, server notes
├── scripts/
│   ├── fake-lsp-server.bb        fake content-length-framed LSP server (validation)
│   ├── validate-client.bb        handshake/requests/notifications/shutdown checks
│   ├── validate-config.bb        config merge + effective registry + root resolution + language invariant
│   └── e2e.bb                    headless tool-executor smoke
└── src/
    ├── extensions/lsp_adapter.clj          entry: init/shutdown, state, registrations, /lsp
    └── extensions/lsp_adapter/
        ├── config.clj      lsp.edn load/merge/template/write-back
        ├── language.clj    path → languageId
        ├── servers.clj     builtin registry + effective registry + root resolution
        ├── client.clj      handshake, policies, document-sync builders, uri helpers
        ├── manager.clj     connections, doc-sync state, fan-out, backoff
        ├── query.clj       operation dispatch, coordinates, result shaping
        └── diagnostics.clj diagnostics store + rendering
```

Dependencies allowed: `kmet.extension`, `kmet.libs.*` (incl. the new
`kmet.libs.jsonrpc`, plus existing `kmet.libs.process`,
`kmet.libs.edn-store`), `clojure.*`, `babashka.*`,
bundled `cheshire.core` + `clojure.core.async`. **No `deps.edn`.**

Lib registration mechanics (do these when landing step 1 of §16):

1. `kmet.libs.jsonrpc` must pass `kmet.libs.test-self-contained` (no
   `kmet.*` requires).
2. Add it to `libs-library-namespaces` in `src/kmet/app/extensions.clj`
   (~line 807 — its docstring says keep in sync with `src/kmet/libs/`).
3. Register `test/kmet/libs/jsonrpc_test.clj` in `kmet.runner/all-namespaces`.

## 6. Config — `config.clj`

### 6.1 Sources & precedence

- Global: `~/.kmet/agent/lsp.edn`
- Project: `<cwd>/.kmet/lsp.edn` — highest precedence, per-field server
  merge + per-key settings merge (later wins). This is the only file the
  extension writes.
- No other sources, no flags.

Composition: built on `kmet.libs.edn-store` — load =
`(deep-merge (read-edn-map global) (read-edn-map project))`; every write
(§6.4/§6.5) goes through `update-edn-map!` under its file lock. No new
custom lib (§4).

### 6.2 EDN format

```clojure
{:settings {:disabled false              ;; literal true disables the whole extension
            :request-timeout-ms 30000    ;; per-LSP-request bound
            :initialize-timeout-ms 60000
            :idle-timeout 15             ;; minutes; 0 disables reaping
            :diagnostics false}          ;; false | map (§12); Phase 2 knobs live here
 :servers
 {"clojure-lsp" {:command "clojure-lsp"  ;; overrides the builtin entry's argv
                 :initialization-options {}
                 :lifecycle :lazy}
  "rust" {:request-timeout-ms 60000}     ;; overrides settings only — slow first index
  "jdtls" {:disabled true}               ;; removes the builtin entirely
  "clojure-alt" {:command "/opt/lsp/clj-lsp"
                 :extensions ["cljc"]}   ;; REPLACES builtin claims (same-id override)
  "fennel" {:command "fennel-ls"         ;; out-of-tree server: full descriptor
            :args []
            :extensions ["fnl"]
            :root-markers ["flxproject.ni"]
            :initialization-options {}}}}
```

Server keys:

| Key | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `:command` | string or vector | spawn argv base; vector = full argv merged with `:args`. Present + unknown id ⇒ new custom server; present + builtin id ⇒ overrides that builtin's argv |
| `:args` | vector of strings | appended to `:command` |
| `:env` | map | merged over `System/getenv` (bb `:env` replaces — merge manually) |
| `:extensions` | vector of strings | claimed file extensions (dot-less, case-insensitive). On a builtin id this REPLACES the builtin list (principle of least surprise — dirge semantics) |
| `:extend-extensions` | vector | ADDITIVE append, deduped (e.g. add `janet` to clojure-lsp without relisting) |
| `:filenames` | vector | whole-filename claims (`CMakeLists.txt`), case-insensitive |
| `:root-markers` | vector | include markers for the root walk-up; absent ⇒ cwd is the root. Bash-style rootless servers use the file's parent dir (builtin flag, §7.3) |
| `:exclude-root-markers` | vector | hand-off markers (deno.json steals a JS tree) |
| `:root-dir` | string | explicit workspace root; skips the walk entirely |
| `:initialization-options` | map | sent verbatim as `initializationOptions` |
| `:request-timeout-ms` | number | overrides the settings default |
| `:lifecycle` | `:lazy` (default) \| `:eager` \| `:keep-alive` | `:eager`/`:keep-alive` connect at `:session-start`; `:keep-alive` is exempt from reaping |
| `:idle-timeout` | number | per-server reaper override (minutes) |
| `:disabled` | bool | only literal `true` acts |

A config entry for an unknown id **without** `:command` is ignored but shown
as `misconfigured` in `/lsp status`.

### 6.3 Key normalization

Known keys accepted in camel or kebab form (copying a pi/opencode-style JSON
config is a light edit): `:settings`/`:servers`, `:requestTimeoutMs`,
`:initializeTimeoutMs`, `:idleTimeout`, `:initializationOptions`,
`:rootMarkers`, `:excludeRootMarkers`, `:rootDir`, `:extendExtensions`.
Values accept string or keyword for enums. Unknown keys pass through.

### 6.4 Template creation

At init, if `~/.kmet/agent/lsp.edn` does not exist, write a
schema-commented starter (one builtin override, one custom server, settings
block). Project `.kmet/lsp.edn` is created only by the first
enable/disable write (§6.5).

### 6.5 enable/disable write

Same semantics as mcp-adapter §6.5, onto `.kmet/lsp.edn`: disable sets
`:disabled true` (creating the entry if absent); enable removes `:disabled`
(writing `:disabled false` instead when the lower-precedence file still
disables it); empty entries are pruned; pretty EDN with trailing newline;
returns `{:path … :changed bool}`; the command tells the user to `/reload`
(or use `/lsp refresh`).

## 7. Detection — `language.clj` + `servers.clj`

One query resolves three questions: which language, which server(s), which
root — then spawn-or-reuse (§10).

### 7.1 Path → languageId (`language.clj`)

Port of dirge `language.rs`: lowercased-extension lookup; extension-less
files match whole filenames (`Makefile` → `makefile`, `Dockerfile`);
unknown → `"plaintext"` so every `didOpen` carries a well-formed payload.
Table lifted from dirge (covers clj cljs cljc edn bb, ts/tsx/js/jsx, py,
go, c/cpp family, m/mm, java, rb, sh/bash/zsh, json/yaml/toml/md/html/css,
nix, swift, zig, cmake, …). **Invariant (unit-tested)**: every extension
claimed by any builtin server must have a languageId entry — dirge shipped
twice with a claimed-but-unmapped extension and the server silently
answered nothing.

### 7.2 Builtin registry (`servers.clj`)

Static descriptors. All entries best-effort: a missing binary surfaces in
status, nothing crashes.

| id | argv | claims (extensions) | root markers | notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `clojure-lsp` | `["clojure-lsp"]` | clj cljs cljc edn bb | deps.edn, project.clj, shadow-cljs.edn, bb.edn, .clj-kondo | |
| `typescript-language-server` | `["typescript-language-server" "--stdio"]` | ts tsx mts cts js jsx mjs cjs | package.json, tsconfig.json, jsconfig.json, package-lock.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, yarn.lock, bun.lock, bun.lockb | exclude: deno.json, deno.jsonc (hand-off) |
| `pyright-langserver` | `["pyright-langserver" "--stdio"]` | py pyi | pyproject.toml, setup.py, setup.cfg, requirements.txt, pyrightconfig.json, Pipfile | |
| `rust-analyzer` | `["rust-analyzer"]` | rs | Cargo.toml | prefers the manifest containing `[workspace]` (walk past nested member crates; literal substring match, dirge's accepted tradeoff) |
| `gopls` | `["gopls" "serve"]` | go | go.mod, go.work | |
| `clangd` | `["clangd"]` | c cc cpp cxx ixx h hh hpp hxx m mm | compile_commands.json, .clangd, CMakeLists.txt, Makefile, meson.build | |
| `ruby-lsp` | `["ruby-lsp"]` | rb rake gemspec | Gemfile, Rakefile, .rubocop.yml, config.ru | |
| `bash-language-server` | `["bash-language-server" "start"]` | sh bash zsh | *(none)* | rootless: root = the file's parent dir |
| `jdtls` | `["jdtls"]` | java | pom.xml, build.gradle, build.gradle.kts, settings.gradle, settings.gradle.kts | JDK-heavy; expected unused on Termux |

Matching: file extension ∈ `:extensions` (lowercased) OR whole filename ∈
`:filenames`. Earlier registry entries win ties when two servers claim the
same extension.

### 7.3 Effective registry + root resolution

Effective registry = builtins, minus `:disabled true` entries, overridden
in place by same-id config entries (`:extensions` replaces;
`:extend-extensions` appends deduped; `:command`/`:args`/markers/options
override), plus custom config entries appended after builtins.

Root resolution — port of `nearest_root`:

1. Canonicalize the queried file; determine the boundary: cwd when the file
   is under cwd, else `fs/home`.
2. If the file is outside the boundary, bail to "boundary = file's own
   directory" (never walk past the boundary — dirge's symlink guard).
3. Walk up from the file's parent: per directory, check
   `:exclude-root-markers` first (hand-off), then `:root-markers` — hit ⇒
   that directory.
4. Boundary reached without a hit ⇒ the boundary itself (single-file
   projects still get a server attached).
5. `:root-dir` in config skips the walk. Rootless servers (flagged builtin
   or no `:root-markers`): root = the file's parent dir.

### 7.4 Spawn-or-reuse

Key `(server-id, root-str)`. Live conn ⇒ reuse. Else, under the server's
lock: cheap `(fs/which command)` first — a miss records a distinct *"not
installed"* failure (better UX than dirge's learn-on-spawn); spawn +
handshake; success clears any broken mark, failure sets it.

**Learned-broken, sticky until reset**: a failed claim — which-miss, spawn
error, or handshake failure — marks the server broken with its reason
(`:not-installed` | `:spawn-failed` + stderr tail). There is **no
time-based retry**: every later query against a claimed file returns the
cached failure instantly (no lock, no which check, no spawn). The mark is
cleared only by an explicit reset — `/lsp restart <name>`, `/lsp refresh`
(a registry rebuild; a changed `:command`/`:args` deserves a fresh
attempt), or `/reload`. Session switches do NOT clear it — binary
availability doesn't change with the session. Zero processes at startup
unless `:lifecycle :eager/:keep-alive`.

A file whose language nobody claims yields a clean
`(no LSP server for .<ext>)` — no spawn attempt is ever made.

## 8. Shared lib — `kmet.libs.jsonrpc`

JSON-RPC 2.0 plumbing for stdio-speaking protocols (extracted up front —
the dirge lesson; its `lsp/rpc.rs` sits on exactly such a shared core).
Protocol-agnostic: MCP/LSP specifics stay in callers.

### 8.1 Framing (pure functions, heavily tested)

```clojure
(encode-content-length payload-string)   ; => bytes to write: header + UTF-8 body
(read-content-length input-stream)       ; => payload-string (blocks for exact N bytes)
(encode-line-msg payload-string)         ; newline-delimited variant (MCP style)
(read-line-msg reader)
```

- `Content-Length` counts **UTF-8 bytes, never chars** — encode first, then
  count the byte array; reads take exactly N bytes off the InputStream and
  decode after accumulation. THE classic LSP client bug; centralized here.
- Header parse: case-insensitive field names, tolerate `\r\n\r\n` and bare
  `\n\n` terminators, ignore `Content-Type` (`application/vscode-jsonrpc;
  charset=utf-8` et al.).

### 8.2 Connection

```clojure
(connect-stdio {:command :args :env :cwd
                :framing :content-length | :line-delimited
                :on-notification (fn [msg])            ; notifications (has :method, no :id)
                :on-request      (fn [method params])  ; server→client requests; return
                                                       ; result map, or nil ⇒ -32601
                :stderr-tail-lines n})                 ; default 20
(request! conn method params & [{:keys [timeout-ms]}]) ; => :result; throws ex-info on
                                                       ; JSON-RPC error / timeout / death
(notify!  conn method params)
(close!   conn & [{:keys [graceful]}])
(alive? conn)  (last-used conn)  (stderr-tail conn)
```

- Reader thread (daemon) parses frames and classifies: **response** (has
  `:id` in pending) delivers its promise and removes it; stale/unknown ids
  are dropped; **server request** (`:method` + `:id`) is answered
  immediately — `:on-request`'s return value as `:result`, nil as
  `{ :code -32601 :message "Method not found: <method>" }`, a throwing
  handler as `-32603` internal error; **notification** goes to
  `:on-notification` (exceptions swallowed, logged to the tail).
- EOF on stdout: mark closed, fail every pending request with
  `ex-info "... connection closed"` `{:type ::transport-dead}` — so
  `request!` distinguishes *timeout* from *process died*.
- `request!`: register `{id → promise}` in an atom, write the frame, deref
  with deadline. Every `request!`/`notify!` bumps `:last-used` (reaper feed).
- `close!`: default kills the process tree immediately
  (`kmet.libs.process`: `collect-descendant-pids` + `kill-process-tree!` —
  npx/jvm-style children must not orphan). `{:graceful
  {:request "shutdown" :notification "exit"}}` sends the polite LSP dance
  first (bounded 2 s), then kills regardless. MCP passes no `:graceful`.
- Self-containment: requires only babashka.process, cheshire.core,
  clojure.java.io, clojure.string — no `kmet.*`, no core.async
  (correlation is promise-per-id; no channel needed).
- Pending-map mutations (`register` / `remove-on-response` /
  `fail-all`) are guarded by the write lock rather than swap-vals!: sci's
  `swap-vals!` silently drops the reset value (atom left nil), which
  broke EOF delivery until the lock pattern replaced it.
- `connect-streams` is public on purpose: it is the stream-injection seam
  tests use in place of subprocesses (and a future hook point for any
  socket transport). Default kill is `babashka.process/destroy-tree`; the
  extension layer additionally registers pids with `kmet.libs.process`
  at spawn time.

### 8.3 Lib tests (`test/kmet/libs/jsonrpc_test.clj`, in-repo gates)

Frame round-trips with multi-byte UTF-8 payloads (byte-count regression);
chunked/split stream reads; `\r\n` vs `\n` headers; out-of-order and stale
responses; `-32601` fallback and `-32603` on throwing handlers; EOF fails
pending requests (timeout-vs-death distinction); graceful shutdown emits
request+notification before killing; line-delimited mode end-to-end against
an in-process fake (piped streams, no subprocess needed for most cases).

## 9. LSP client layer — `client.clj`

Thin protocol adapter over the lib.

### 9.1 Handshake

`initialize` (settings `:initialize-timeout-ms`, default 60 s):

```clojure
{:processId <pid or nil>
 :rootUri  (path->uri root)            ; also :rootPath (deprecated, harmless)
 :capabilities {...§9.2...}
 :initializationOptions (:initialization-options definition {})
 :workspaceFolders [{:uri (path->uri root) :name (fs/file-name root)}]}
```

then `initialized` notification. Record `serverInfo` (name/version) for
status display.

File URIs: `(str (.toUri (fs/path p)))` interop — correct percent-encoding
(spaces, unicode Android paths) without any `java.nio.file` import; the
reverse strips `file://` and URL-decodes.

### 9.2 Client capabilities (conservative, static)

```clojure
{:textDocument {:synchronization {:dynamicRegistration false}
                :publishDiagnostics {:relatedInformation false
                                     :versionSupport true}}
 :workspace {:configuration true
             :workspaceFolders true
             :didChangeConfiguration {:dynamicRegistration false}}}
```

Full-text sync assumed; servers that need more degrade gracefully.

### 9.3 Notification routing

- `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` → the diagnostics store callback (§12).
- `window/logMessage`, `window/showMessage` → bounded ring (rendered in
  `/lsp status` failure detail alongside stderr tails).
- everything else (`$/progress`, `$/logTrace`, `textDocument/*` partial
  results) → dropped.

### 9.4 Server-request policy

| Method | Reply |
|---|---|
| `workspace/configuration` | vector of `nil` per requested item (defaults) |
| `client/registerCapability` | `{}` (accept, ignore) |
| `window/workDoneProgress/create` | `{}` |
| `workspace/applyEdit` | `{:applied false :failureReason "kmet edits files itself"}` — servers must never write through us |
| anything else | nil ⇒ lib replies `-32601` |

### 9.5 Document-sync builders

`did-open` (uri, languageId via `language.clj`, version 1, full text),
`did-change` (full-text single content change, version inc),
`did-close`, `did-save`. Builders here; ownership/versioning state in the
manager.

## 10. Manager — `manager.clj`

State (per extension instance):

```clojure
{:servers {name {:definition {}
                 :roots   (atom {"<root-str>" conn})
                 :failed-at (atom nil)   ; epoch-ms of last failure
                 :error    (atom nil)    ; last failure message
                 :lock     (Object.)}}}
;; conn = {:client   <lib conn>
;;         :root     path
;;         :docs     (atom {path version})     ; open-document versions
;;         :diags    (atom {uri {:diagnostics [...] :received-at ms}})
;;         }
```

- `claiming-servers path` → `[{name definition root}]` over the effective
  registry (§7).
- `ensure-connected! name root` — locked, idempotent; which-check; spawn via
  lib; handshake; wire §9.3/§9.4 policies scoped to this conn; broken-mark
  bookkeeping (§7.4).
- `touch-file! conn path` — read from disk; unopened ⇒ `didOpen`;
  otherwise `didChange` full-text, `version++`. Re-reading disk on every
  touch means kmet's own edits are picked up without watching the FS.
  Positional queries touch with **Notify** semantics — no diagnostic wait
  (that's Phase 2's edit-hook concern, dirge's note verbatim).
- Fan-out: for each claiming conn — touch, request, collect. Per-server
  errors are logged into the section output, never fatal; all-empty ⇒
  `(no results)`. Sequential across conns (requests pipeline safely;
  typically ≤2 servers claim a file).
- `disconnect-server! name root` — `didClose` all open docs, graceful
  shutdown dance, tree-kill, clear conn. `shutdown-all!` for unload.
- Reaper support: `last-used` from the lib; the daemon lives in the entry.

## 11. Query tool — `query.clj`

### 11.1 Operations

| Operation | Aliases | LSP method | Needs | Answers |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `definition` | `goToDefinition` | `textDocument/definition` | pos | Where is this symbol defined |
| `references` | `findReferences` | `textDocument/references` | pos | Every reference (`includeDeclaration: true`) |
| `hover` | | `textDocument/hover` | pos | Docs/type signature |
| `documentSymbol` | | `textDocument/documentSymbol` | file | File outline |
| `workspaceSymbol` | | `workspace/symbol` | file + `query` | Project-wide symbol search |
| `implementation` | `goToImplementation` | `textDocument/implementation` | pos | Implementors |
| `prepareCallHierarchy` | | `textDocument/prepareCallHierarchy` | pos | Call-hierarchy seed item |
| `incomingCalls` | | `callHierarchy/incomingCalls` | pos | Callers (two-step: prepare → incoming) |
| `outgoingCalls` | | `callHierarchy/outgoingCalls` | pos | Callees (two-step) |
| `diagnostics` | | *(store read)* | file | Current published diagnostics |

Position ops take `line`/`character` **1-based**; the subtraction happens
once, here (dirge's drift lesson: aliases and conversion share this single
dispatch point). `callHierarchy/incoming/outgoing` send `{:item <first
prepare-result>}` — the prepare round-trip is internal to one tool call.

### 11.2 Parameters (JSON schema)

```json
{"operation": {"type": "string", "enum": [...§11.1...] },
 "filePath":  {"type": "string", "description": "Absolute preferred; resolved against cwd"},
 "line":      {"type": "number", "description": "1-based"},
 "character": {"type": "number", "description": "1-based"},
 "query":     {"type": "string", "description": "workspaceSymbol search"}}
```

Required: `operation`, `filePath`. Position validation errors name the
missing field and the operation's needs.

### 11.3 Result shaping (token economy)

- Locations (definition/references/implementation) → deduped
  `<rel-path>:<line>:<col>` lines, cap 50 + `… and N more`; paths displayed
  relative to cwd when under it.
- Hover → contents flattened (string / `{:value}` / array joined), trimmed
  at 2000 chars.
- Symbols (document/workspace) → `name kind:line` lines, hierarchical
  flattened, cap 50.
- Call hierarchy → `caller-name kind @ path:line (N call sites)`.
- Multi-server sections labelled `── <server> (<root>) ──`; per-server
  failures listed at the end; empty overall ⇒ `(no results)`.
- Servers answering `nil` normalize to empty (common for positional ops).

Tool description mirrors dirge's `DESCRIPTION` (~150 tokens): operation
list, position conventions, `(no results)` note, "raw-ish but shaped"
promise, plus the lazy cold-start line ("first call on a language spawns
its server and may take seconds while it indexes"). Error-prone
conventions live in parameter descriptions — notably `line`/`character`
"1-based, as shown in editors", the known model footgun.

**No skill ships with the extension** (mcp-adapter ships one because proxy
discovery is non-inferable; `lsp`'s vocabulary is editor-native and the
tool description carries the contract — a skill would be pure context
overhead). Gate: if the §15.7 real-world smoke shows convention fumbles,
promote a compact `skills/lsp/SKILL.md` in Phase 2 via
`:resources-discover`.

## 12. Diagnostics — `diagnostics.clj`

### 12.1 Store

`publishDiagnostics` notifications swap into the owning conn's `:diags`
atom: `{uri {:diagnostics [...] :received-at epoch-ms}}`. Version-aware
(`versionSupport`) — stale pushes for older versions are ignored when the
doc is tracked.

### 12.2 Rendering (dirge `diagnostic.rs` caps)

`pretty`: `SEVERITY [line:col] message (source)` — 1-based coordinates;
severity 1/2/3/4 → ERROR/WARN/INFO/HINT, absent ⇒ ERROR.

- Per-file view (`operation: "diagnostics"`): cap 8 rendered, overflow
  `… and N more`.
- Flood guard: ≥40 errors in one file ⇒ one-line summary instead (a flood
  is almost never caused by the agent — dumping a wall of noise is the
  opposite of useful).
- Project view: ≤5 additional files beyond the queried one, sorted by
  error count desc.

### 12.3 Phase 2 — after-edit hook (specified, gated by `settings :diagnostics {:after-edit true}`, default off)

`ext/on-tool-result` fires for `edit`/`write` with the tool's `:args` in
the hook payload (verified: `loop.clj` `after-tool-hook-result` passes
`{:tool-call-id :tool-name :args :result :is-error}`) — **no core change
needed**. Flow: extract the edited `:path` → claiming servers → touch
(await-push semantics): send the sync, then wait up to
`:wait-ms` (default 4000) for a fresh `publishDiagnostics`
(`received-at > t0`); on timeout report whatever is stored (cold-start
servers simply report stale-or-empty rather than blocking forever — the
pull-diagnostics race is the Phase-2 refinement). Append a capped
`<diagnostics>` block to the tool result content.

## 13. Entry — `lsp_adapter.clj`

Init order (all no-ops when `settings :disabled true`):

1. Load config; create the global template when missing.
2. State atom (§10 shape) + api ref.
3. Register the `lsp` tool (description §11.3, schema §11.2) with the
   contextual contract — the execute fn polls the run's abort signal
   between request waits (§13 Lifecycle edges).
4. Register `/lsp` with argument completions (subcommands, then server
   names).
5. Start the idle-reaper daemon (30 s ticks; skip `:keep-alive`; honor
   per-server `:idle-timeout`; 0 disables; skips servers holding their
   connect lock — never reap mid-initialize).
6. Footer status: `ui-set-status api "lsp"` — compact summary
   (`🔌 LSP: clojure-lsp@~/kmet` or `🔌 LSP: 2 servers`), cleared when no
   servers are configured/running; inert in headless mode.
7. Events: `:session-start` (any reason) → background eager/keep-alive
   connects (daemon thread, idempotent — live conns no-op, never blocks);
   `:session-shutdown` → full teardown (`shutdown-all!` + reaper stop)
   **only for `:reason :quit`**. On `:new`/`:resume`/`:fork` do nothing:
   kmet fires shutdown/start around every session switch (event_bus.clj),
   and servers are workspace-scoped — killing them would force a cold
   re-index after every `/new`.

`shutdown` (unload/reload): stop reaper, `shutdown-all!` (graceful dance +
tree-kill), deregistration is automatic.

Lifecycle edges:

- **ESC / run interrupt**: the tool honors the run's abort signal —
  in-flight request waits are abandoned promptly (the result is discarded
  by the host anyway); the LSP process is NOT killed — cached
  infrastructure, warm for the next call. Late responses arrive as stale
  replies and drop in the lib.
- **Session switch** (`/new`, `/resume`, tree fork): nothing torn down.
  Conns, doc versions, diagnostics stores and learned-broken marks all
  persist — workspace truth didn't change, and the disk re-read per touch
  self-heals document state.
- **`/reload`**: full unload path above; next use starts completely fresh
  (learned-broken marks included).

`/lsp` subcommands:

| Subcommand | Effect |
|---|---|
| *(bare)* / `status` | servers, states (connected / idle / broken+reason / disabled / misconfigured), roots, open-doc counts, recent log tail — text dialog (TUI) or println (headless) |
| `list [server]` | registry entries + claims + markers |
| `restart <name>` | clear the learned-broken mark, disconnect all roots, reconnect on next claim |
| `enable\|disable <name>` | write-back §6.5; suggests `/reload` |
| `refresh` | reload `lsp.edn` live: drop removed/disabled conns, rebuild the effective registry |

## 14. README

Enabling (symlink `extensions/lsp-adapter` into `~/.kmet/agent/extensions/`
or `.kmet/extensions/`), first-run template note, EDN config reference
(server keys table, builtin registry table), the `lsp` tool reference with
examples, `/lsp` reference, lifecycle notes (lazy spawn, backoff, idle
reaping), per-language install hints (`clojure-lsp`, `typescript-language-
server`, … — "install the binary, done"), security note (LSP servers run
with your user privileges and index your code — configure only servers you
trust), Phase-2 roadmap.

## 15. Validation plan

1. **Lib unit tests** (`test/kmet/libs/jsonrpc_test.clj`, in-repo gates —
   §8.3 list).
2. **Fake LSP server** (`scripts/fake-lsp-server.bb`): content-length
   framing; `initialize` reply advertising full-text sync +
   `textDocumentDefinitionProvider` etc.; `initialized` ack; canned
   `textDocument/definition` (a fixed Location), `documentSymbol` (nested),
   `workspace/symbol`; a `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` push after the
   first `didOpen`; a `workspace/configuration` server-request asserting the
   client answers; handles the `shutdown`→`exit` dance; clean exit 0.
3. **Client validation** (`validate-client.bb`, fake server): handshake,
   each operation, notification capture, server-request auto-reply, EOF
   failing pending requests, graceful shutdown, restart cycle, stderr-tail
   capture, broken-mark stickiness (a failed claim ⇒ the second query is
   served from the cache with no spawn attempt).
4. **Config validation** (`validate-config.bb`): precedence merge,
   camel/kebab normalization, template creation, enable/disable round-trip
   (incl. lower-source-disabled case), effective-registry computation
   (override/extend/disable/custom/misconfigured), root-resolution fixtures
   (temp dirs with marker files, incl. deno hand-off and boundary
   fallback), language-table invariant.
5. **Nullable-api load check**: `init` against
   `kmet.extension/create-nullable-api` — tool, command, event
   registrations present; `:disabled` settings ⇒ nothing registered;
   `shutdown` tears down cleanly.
6. **e2e** (`e2e.bb`): headless — drive the registered tool's `execute`
   directly against the fake server (definition/hover/diagnostics/status
   flows), like mcp-adapter's headless smoke.
7. **Real-world smoke**: clojure-lsp on this repo (`deps.edn` marker) —
   definition/hover/documentSymbol/workspaceSymbol/diagnostics on
   `src/kmet/app/extensions.clj`; record results in the README.
8. **Quality**: manual clj-kondo + cljfmt over the extension files
   (`bb lint-changed` covers the lib + dependents), plan/README
   consistency.

## 16. Implementation order

1. `kmet.libs.jsonrpc` + unit tests; register in
   `libs-library-namespaces` + `kmet.runner/all-namespaces`; gates green.
2. `config.clj` (+ §15.4 pieces).
3. `language.clj` + `servers.clj` (tables, effective registry, root
   resolution + fixture tests).
4. `client.clj` (handshake, policies, builders, uri helpers) validated
   against the fake server.
5. `manager.clj` (connections, doc sync, fan-out, backoff).
6. `query.clj` + tool registration; `diagnostics.clj` store + op.
7. Entry `lsp_adapter.clj` (state, `/lsp`, events, status, reaper) +
   completions.
8. Scripts polish, README, real-world smoke (§15.7).

Phase 2 lands separately after Phase 1 settles: after-edit hook → panel →
incremental sync → (optional) mcp-adapter stdio adoption.

## 17. Risks & notes

- **Content-Length counts bytes, not chars** — centralized in the lib; never
  hand-roll framing at call sites.
- Extension sci context: no futures — daemon threads via the copied `spawn`
  helper; exceptions in daemons swallowed deliberately.
- bb `:env` replaces the environment — merge `System/getenv` manually.
- `:pid` absent on bb process records — `(.pid (:proc p))`.
- First-touch indexing latency: cold clojure-lsp/jdtls can exceed casual
  expectations — initialize bounded at 60 s, requests at 30 s; timeouts are
  retryable, while the broken mark applies to spawn/handshake failures only
  and sticks until an explicit reset (§7.4) — a slow-but-healthy server is
  never marked broken mid-index.
- Parallel tool calls race first-connect — per-server lock serializes;
  post-handshake requests are id-matched and safe to pipeline.
- Termux reality: most servers are absent; the `fs/which` pre-check makes
  "not installed" a first-class status, and nothing attempts spawns for
  unclaimed languages.
- File URIs on Android paths (spaces, unicode): `(.toUri (fs/path …))`
  interop; no `java.io.*`/`java.nio.file` imports (AGENTS convention).
- Full-text `didChange` always (simplest correct); disk re-read per touch;
  incremental sync only if profiling ever demands it (Phase 2).
- `workspace/applyEdit` refused by policy — a server that insists will show
  `applied: false` in its logs; our edits flow exclusively through kmet's
  edit tools.
- Large results: shaping caps (§11.3) keep responses bounded; no byte-level
  output guard needed.
- Extension files sit outside `bb lint` — keep them clj-kondo-clean manually;
  the lib enjoys the full gates (this asymmetry is why the risky code lives
  in the lib).
- Windows: header tolerance for `\r\n`; process-tree kill already proven by
  mcp-adapter.

## 18. Implementation notes & recorded deviations

### Phase 1 step 1 — kmet.libs.jsonrpc (implemented)

- **No core.async**: the plan's dependency list carried over from
  mcp-adapter out of habit; promise-per-id correlation needs no channel.
  Lib requires only babashka.process, cheshire, clojure.java.io,
  clojure.string.
- **Lock-guarded pending map instead of swap-vals!**: discovered during
  testing that sci's `swap-vals!` returns `[old nil]` and leaves the atom
  nil (reset value lost) — an EOF'd connection therefore delivered
  nothing and requests hung until timeout. All pending mutations now run
  under `(:write-lock conn)`; clj-kondo-clean via bind-before-locking.
- **`connect-streams` is public** (contract said "the seam tests use" but
  didn't mark visibility): private would trip clj-kondo in the tests;
  doubles as the future socket-transport hook.
- Tests: 17 deftests / 41 assertions over piped streams, ~0.6s total;
  registered in `kmet.runner/all-namespaces` as `kmet.libs.test-jsonrpc`;
  lib registered in `libs-library-namespaces`.
